{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And you shall make.</b> We find written קדמה מזרחה (below, verse 13), and we know that the heads of the east are three: one corresponding to the point of the head of Capricorn, which is the end of the sun's inclination toward the south; and the second corresponding to the equator, which is the head of Aries and Libra; and the third corresponding to the head of Cancer, which is the end of the sun's inclination toward the north. And thus נגבה תימנה דרום." "<b>And southward.</b> From the root of ימין צפון and ימין אתה בראתם (Psalms 89:13)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "Resolved the verse citation למטה פ' יג to 'below, verse 13'; the reference is to Exodus 27:13, later in the same chapter."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:43.289758125Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}